# Zealakit Agent Plugin Flow conventions

- `packages/core` is the only source of the protocol, platform fragments, `coder.json`
  template and icon. Never edit a generated copy (`SKILL.md`, `protocol.js`, the
  `config/coder.example.json` files, `icon.svg`, the `CODER_TEMPLATE` block of `client.js`);
  edit core, run `pnpm sync`, commit both.
- Platform packages are self-contained when installed: no runtime import from `packages/core`.
- Every platform keeps the same five ⏸ gate lines, word for word. Platform differences go in
  `packages/core/platforms/<platform>/*.md` only. Run `pnpm check:parity`.
- The protocol names no vendor, provider, model, or CLI. Never read, print, store, or commit
  an API key; config holds the name of an environment variable.
- Never weaken an approval gate or infer an approval from files on disk. Only the user's own `--approve-all` pre-approves gates 1-3, never the commit.
- The Harness has no build step: plain JavaScript ESM, no JSX, no bundler, JSDoc for types.
  The Claude plugin is Markdown and JSON only.
- The command, skill and plugin are `zlak-flow`; the project-side folder is `.zlak-flow/`;
  packages are `@zealakit/agent-plugin-flow-*`. Do not reintroduce `zl-*`, `zap-*` or
  `agent-plugins`. Files and folders are `kebab-case`.
- Biome formats; run `pnpm lint:fix`. Tests use `node:test` only: do not add a second test
  framework. New behavior ships with a focused test in the owning package.
- One shared version, changed only with `pnpm set-version <v>`.
- No `docs/` folder. Documentation lives in the root and package READMEs. Load
  `.agents/skills/readme-system/SKILL.md` before touching any README.
- Verify with `pnpm check` before reporting work as done.
- Agents never publish, tag, push a tag, or create a release; there is no CI publishing.
- Load `.agents/skills/agent-plugin-flow/SKILL.md` before code, test, docs, or release work.
